From 2dcb4b8f290ce84acf99b8b304d2e19050be3720 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 16:30:15 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Remote casting through the lens, and The Hand (building slice
 12b)

When the wizard is not on the board, any fielded ally's tray shows The
Lens: the wizard casts a spell from their own deck through that ally,
from the campus. A remote spell never deals damage: what qualifies is
derived from the spell's effects (an allowlist of movement, terrain and
hazard, protection, cleansing, non-damaging conditions and intent
reading), never from an authored flag.

- RemoteCasting.cs: reach (dive, or a defense), budget (1 a fight, 2 with
  The Hand), 2 Essence in a dive, the damage-free test, the spell list.
- CombatManager.RemoteCast.cs: tray card, spell picker, aiming from the
  ally, casting through the item seam (mana waived, no AP).
- Tray, arming, cancel and click routing know the armed remote spell.
- The Hand (Scrying Chambers T3) unblocked: two casts a fight, and the
  lens reaches posting defenses and castle defenses before the wizard
  arrives. Scrying Chambers T1 text names the lens.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RF7HNp6pvyXiAz229q52Px
